    "q-351582": {
      "dom_id": "step-q351582",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{e}^{-3|x|+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "We break up the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{e}^{-3|x|+2}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{-3|x|+2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-3|x|+2}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nEvaluating the first of these integrals, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{-3|x|+2} & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{0}{e}^{3x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3x+2}\\,{|}_{a}^{0}\\,) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }(\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3a+2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the integrand ${e}^{-3|x|+2}$ is an **even** function. This means that we can immediately deduce that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-3|x|+2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since both improper integrals exist, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{e}^{-3|x|+2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}{e}^{-3|x|+2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-3|x|+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{e}^{2}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{2}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
